# v19 verification log — mismatch breakdown, standardization-claim scoping, terminology sync, log-date fix
# Date: 2026-09-02 (UTC)

## Changes in v19 (relative to v18, external review follow-up)

1. Mismatch breakdown made explicit. Independently recomputed with the
   packaged compute_unified_difficulty.py against the design-time labels of
   main_evaluation_dataset.jsonl (245 rows):
     match 144, mismatch 101, of which 92 (91.1%) adjacent-stratum,
     9 non-adjacent.
   §2.1.2 and the untranslated-EN-25 paragraph now state
   「不一致101件のうち92件（91.1%）は隣接層間のずれ」 (with the 9 non-adjacent
   cases noted in §2.1.2) instead of 「不一致はほぼ隣接層間のずれ」.

2. Standardization claim scoped. §4.3.1 now reads: the 5.5 pp standardized
   difference means the gap is not explained *by the 4-stratum difficulty
   composition alone*; within-stratum structural complexity (SQL length,
   table count, subquery count) and few-shot coverage remain uncontrolled,
   and the standardized comparison stays an exploratory observation.

3. Terminology sync in the reproduction package. README_PACKAGE.md no longer
   says 「統一複雑さスコア」: it now calls compute_unified_difficulty.py a
   post-hoc proxy approximating the design-time structural-complexity
   criterion (not the deterministic generator of the historical labels), with
   the same 144/245 + 92/101 (91.1%) breakdown. The script's docstring header
   was changed from "Unified complexity score" to "Post-hoc
   structural-complexity proxy" with the same caveat. The file name is kept.

4. v18 log date fix: the v18 verification log header/section erroneously said
   2026-06-02 (template/seed carry-over); corrected to 2026-09-02, matching
   paper_data.json generated_at and the compiled PDF. The v18 log's
   `grep -rn difficulty_unified: 0 hits` claim is now scoped as "excluding
   verification_logs/" since the logs themselves mention the old name when
   describing the rename.

No model outputs, saved runs, statistics, or SSOT numeric values changed in
v19; the edits are wording/documentation plus the recomputed (deterministic)
mismatch breakdown.

